A||||3||mbramble||Sun Visors -- Help!!||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||05-11-2001||08:44 AM||||This may be quite simple but it is driving me crazy!!  There were 5 or 6 sun visors in my GT project car when I bought it.  On some the visor itself has been removed from the mount/arm.  I just replaced the headliner and was trying to install a "set" of the visors.  I can't get the blasted things mounted properly.  I can't tell which is left or right and which way the mounting base should be positioned in order to allow the visor to fit in it's "closed" position and then to swing away towards the window.  <P>Are they left/right specific??  Some of them have a "1" stamped on the underside of the mount, others have a "2".  How should the base be oriented when it is mounted to allow the visors to move properly.  It can be twisted 360 degrees and I'm pretty sure all have been twisted from their original location.<P>Any help would be greatly appreciated!!!!<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-11-2001||09:46 AM||||Mike. I'll <I>try</I> to describe this. <BR>I believe the mounts can swap, left to right. When the mount is in position, the shaft that the visor swings on should be straight up and down. <BR>If you hold the visor in the normal "down" position, with the mount rotated so the swivel is pointed straight up, then the mounting flange should taper "away" from the center of the cabin. In other words, the highest part of the lip will be closest to the center of the car. The lowest part of the lip will be towards the A-pillar. <BR>Does this make any sense at all?<BR>If it's a brand new headliner, it's gonna be a lot of fun finding where the holes go.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||05-11-2001||10:46 AM||||Thanks Steve.  I will look at it all when I get home this afternoon.  I found the holes -- on the driver's side anyway -- as I have mounted the thing probably 10 different times.  Finally had to give up before I tried to put my fist thru the windshield out of frustration!!!<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||05-11-2001||09:21 PM||||Well, I think the description helped -- I got them mounted properly anyway!!  My wife is right now making new covers for the visors out of the headliner material I just used.<P>Thanks much for the help!!<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
